  "result": "Perfect! All **305 tests pass** \u2713\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added foreign currency support to `src/money.js` with the following additions:\n\n### Implementation Details\n\n**1. RATES Constant**\n```javascript\nexport const RATES = { EUR: 1, USD: 1.085, GBP: 0.8425 };\n```\nDefines exchange rates (units of that currency per euro)\n\n**2. `convert(cents, currency)` Function**\n- Takes EUR cents and target currency code\n- Multiplies by exchange rate\n- Rounds to integer cents using `roundCents()`\n- Returns `ok(convertedCents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n- Examples:\n  - `convert(10000, 'USD')` \u2192 \u20ac100 = $108.50 (10850 cents)\n  - `convert(10000, 'GBP')` \u2192 \u20ac100 = \u00a384.25 (8425 cents)\n\n**3. `formatMoney(cents, currency)` Function**\n- Formats cents with proper currency symbol ($, \u00a3, \u20ac)\n- Adds thousands separators\n- Shows 2 decimal places\n- Examples:\n  - `formatMoney(123456, 'USD')` \u2192 `$1,234.56`\n  - `formatMoney(123456, 'GBP')` \u2192 `\u00a31,234.56`\n  - Defaults to EUR format for unknown currencies\n\n### Test Coverage\n\nAdded **24 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- \u2713 RATES definition verification\n- \u2713 Currency conversion (EUR \u2192 USD, EUR \u2192 GBP, EUR \u2192 EUR)\n- \u2713 Unknown currency error handling\n- \u2713 Edge cases (zero, negative amounts)\n- \u2713 Rounding to integer cents\n- \u2713 formatMoney with all currencies\n- \u2713 Large amounts and thousands separator formatting\n- \u2713 Decimal precision preservation\n- \u2713 Roundtrip conversion and formatting\n- \u2713 Multiple concurrent currency operations\n\n**All 305 tests pass** across the entire project \u2713",
